  "explanation": "Children with significant burns need burn replacement fluid plus separate maintenance fluid because of their ongoing physiological requirements. Oral fluids are usually inadequate for initial resuscitation, and hypotonic saline is not appropriate as a resuscitation fluid. The Parkland formula is not expressed as 3 mL × TBSA × age.",
